# device_version_stamp_index_above_count: A child FIFO whose stamp index (40) was valid when it was defined at version 245 (64 FIFOs) signals nothing once the guest lowers the version to 60 (32 FIFOs): DeviceCore::signal_stamp drops indices above maxFIFOCount, so the stamp slot stays and no interrupt comes; back at 245 the next stamp is published. Index 32 at version 60 is still published: the check is `>`, not `>=`.
